{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:73d642b5966369f0","name":"Nssis-Class Clawcraft","source":{"id":"source:reference-73d642b5966369f0","title":"Nssis-Class Clawcraft","revision":18766,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T20:41:53Z","sha256":"f4306474b6db6da95ae07f1820f8536086e905e7d39176febc63f8701c093c6d","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18766","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Nssis-Class%20Clawcraft&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-73d642b5966369f0","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Chiss Ascendancy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Chiss_Ascendancy","referenceId":"reference:410c64a9afa98052"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Galactic Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Galactic_Empire","referenceId":"reference:f9c9a48674cc3415"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"a","children":["Chiss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Chiss","referenceId":"reference:bd57eaad77f8edcc"}," use the term \"Clawcraft\" to describe a broad class of fast, maneuverable ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighters"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighters","referenceId":"reference:e127af2636e147fc"}," popular with their pilots and with military strategists. In fact, there have been dozens of models of Clawcraft over the history of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Chiss Ascendancy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Chiss_Ascendancy","referenceId":"reference:410c64a9afa98052"},", as would be expected of any long-lasting galactic government. When used by non-",{"tag":"a","children":["Chiss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Chiss","referenceId":"reference:bd57eaad77f8edcc"},", however, the term almost always refers to a ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class Clawcraft, a fusion of Imperial and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Chiss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Chiss","referenceId":"reference:bd57eaad77f8edcc"}," technology.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class Clawcraft can be traced directly to the Imperial forces under the command of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Grand Admiral Thrawn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Grand_Admiral_Thrawn"},". Thrawn had access to ",{"tag":"a","children":["Chiss"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Chiss","referenceId":"reference:bd57eaad77f8edcc"}," technology in the form of his Household Phalanx and to Imperial resources as a Grand Admiral. Sometime after the Battle of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Yavin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Yavin"},", Thrawn began trying to merge these technologies, resulting in custom-built craft using the ball cockpit of the TIE design coupled with the claw-wing design common among Chiss Clawcraft. In time, this design was perfected and standardized, becoming the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class. Rather than being a hybrid or \"",{"tag":"a","children":["Ugly"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ugly"},",\" the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class Clawcraft is a customized fighter design drawing on the strong points of two different lines of technology. The design is so efficient that it sees use with Imperial forces, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Chiss Ascendancy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Chiss_Ascendancy","referenceId":"reference:410c64a9afa98052"},", and the Empire of the Hand.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Capabilities"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["The ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class Clawcraft was intended to be an improvement over the ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Interceptor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Interceptor","referenceId":"reference:d62c9e17ed58a2d1"},". It had similar armament to a ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Interceptor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Interceptor","referenceId":"reference:d62c9e17ed58a2d1"},", but added more armor, modest shields, and a Class 1.5 ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"},". Though not as fast on a straight-out run as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["TIE Interceptor"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/TIE_Interceptor","referenceId":"reference:d62c9e17ed58a2d1"},", the Clawcraft was significantly more maneuverable. With a week of consumables, the ",{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class could do anything a TIE/In could, additionally acting as a long-range scout or attacking far-off targets in large numbers without the aid of a carrier ship.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Early versions of the Clawcraft had neither Astromech Droids nor ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputers"}," to plot hyperspace jumps, instead depending on data from a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Ascendancy Beacon Ship"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Ascendancy_Beacon_Ship?action=edit&redlink=1"},". Such ships could not make a hyperspace jump more than a day away from a beacon ship or similar source of hyperspace coordinates. Later models crammed a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"}," into each Clawcraft.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Expert)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Nssis"]},"-Class Clawcraft Statistics (CL 10)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starfighter"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starfighter"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]},"